      <memberdef kind="function" id="xsecure__libver_8h_1ae22d1d0811abf08bad87a6adb01a7620" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XSecure_GetServerLibInfo</definition>
        <argsstring>(XSecure_ClientInstance *InstancePtr, Xil_LibInfo *LibInfo)</argsstring>
        <name>XSecure_GetServerLibInfo</name>
        <param>
          <type>XSecure_ClientInstance *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Xil_LibInfo *</type>
          <declname>LibInfo</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Queries the XilSecure server (PLM) library information - version and capability bitmaps - by issuing a Features command with an always-present crypto api-id. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the client instance (mailbox handle + SlrIndex). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>LibInfo</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a Xil_LibInfo structure that receives the server library version (LibVersion) and capability bitmap words.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS - On success</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM - If InstancePtr or LibInfo is NULL</para></listitem><listitem><para>Error - On SMC/mailbox transport failure or if the Features command fails</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The Features command is sent with a valid crypto api-id so the server command SUCCEEDS and returns the full response buffer, in which the library version/capability are reported at fixed indices ([3]/[4]). A server too old to report capabilities leaves those words at 0, which the caller reads as &quot;no
        capability advertised&quot; - the safe default. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
