    <briefdescription>
<para>This file contains function prototypes and definitions for the XilSecure client-server library version compatibility check. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The client library is built with a compile-time version (XSECURE_MAJOR_VERSION. XSECURE_MINOR_VERSION from <ref refid="xsecure__ver_8h" kindref="compound">xsecure_ver.h</ref>). The server (PLM) is built with its own version. When the two binaries are produced/updated independently, their versions may diverge. These APIs let a user application query the server library version and verify that the client it is linked against is compatible with the running server before issuing crypto requests.</para><para>Compatibility rule:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Major version MUST match between client and server (a major bump indicates a breaking change).</para></listitem><listitem><para>Client minor version MUST be less than or equal to the server minor version. A newer server stays backward compatible with an older client (an older client only uses features the newer server still supports), so client minor &lt; server minor is acceptable; only client minor &gt; server minor is reported as a minor mismatch.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><preformatted>
MODIFICATION HISTORY:</preformatted></para><para><preformatted>Ver   Who     Date     Changes
<hruler/>

5.8   tus     08/19/26 Initial release with XSecure_GetLibInfo() and capability
                       query helper</preformatted></para><para><preformatted></preformatted> </para>    </detaileddescription>
